        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your 85-year-old male patient, who presented on 23/04/2008 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he exhibited increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed hyperinflation without signs of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy. Continuous pulse oximetry monitoring was maintained throughout. Clinical condition improved satisfactorily, and the patient was discharged on 24/04/2008 in stable condition. Please continue maintenance bronchodilator therapy and ensure close follow-up. Patient education regarding exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
